<span id="values"></span>
== Freedom Values ==
* [https://github.com/Whonix Open Source] -- We respect user rights to review, scrutinize, modify, and redistribute Whonix. This improves security and privacy for everyone.
* [[Reasons for Freedom Software|Freedom Software]] -- Whonix is Freedom Software and contains software developed by the Free Software Foundation and the GNU Project.
* [[What we do|Research and Implementation Project]] -- Whonix is an actively maintained research project making constant improvements; no shortcomings are ever hidden from users.
* [[Reasons for Freedom Software|Fully Auditable]] -- Whonix is independently verifiable by security experts and software developers around the world. This improves security and privacy for everyone.
* [[Deep scan ready|Deep Scan Ready]] -- Whonix supports offline inspection so you can verify storage and boot components from a clean external environment, without trusting the running system.
* [[Reasons for Freedom Software#No Intentional User Freedom Restrictions|Complete respect for privacy and user freedom]] -- Whonix respects data privacy principles. We don't make advertising deals or collect sensitive personal data.

<span id="upcoming"></span>
== Upcoming Security Enhancements ==
* [[Sandbox-app-launcher|sandbox-app-launcher]] -- sandbox-app-launcher is an application launcher that can start each application inside its own restrictive sandbox. Each application runs as its own user, in a bubblewrap sandbox and confined by AppArmor.
* [[Apparmor-profile-everything|Full system Mandatory Access Control (MAC)]] -- Full system Mandatory Access Control (MAC) policy - "AppArmor for everything".
* [https://forums.whonix.org/t/untrusted-root-does-it-make-sense-to-try-to-improve-security-by-restricting-root/7998 Untrusted Root User] -- Restrict root to reduce the impact of compromise.
* [[Dev/VirusForget|Deactivate malware after reboot]] -- Deactivate malware after reboot from non-root compromise.
* [https://github.com/Kicksecure/hardened-kernel Hardened Linux Kernel] -- Hardened Linux Kernel.
* [https://forums.whonix.org/t/use-codecrypt-to-sign-whonix-releases/7844/2 Post-quantum resistance] -- Post-quantum resistant signing of releases.
* [https://forums.whonix.org/t/re-mount-home-and-other-with-noexec-and-nosuid-among-other-useful-mount-options-for-better-security/7707 Mount Options Hardening] -- Mount Options Hardening.
* [https://forums.whonix.org/t/multiple-boot-modes-for-better-security-persistent-root-persistent-noroot-live-root-live-noroot/7708 Multiple boot modes] -- Multiple boot modes for better security (user, live, secureadmin and superadmin).

